---
import StarlightPage from '@astrojs/starlight/components/StarlightPage.astro';
import notes from '../../.generated/notes.json';
import subjectManifests from '../../.generated/subjects.json';
import { buildLibrary } from '../lib/notebook.mjs';

const headings = [
  { depth: 2, slug: 'why-this-notebook-exists', text: 'Why this notebook exists' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'how-i-work', text: 'How I work' },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'what-you-will-find', text: "What you'll find" },
  { depth: 2, slug: 'open-notebook', text: 'An open notebook' },
];
// Read the notebook's own tracks and subjects instead of naming them here, so
// this page stays true when a new track or subject appears in the notes
// repository.
const library = buildLibrary(notes, subjectManifests);
const subjects = new Intl.ListFormat('en', { style: 'long', type: 'conjunction' })
  .format(library.subjects.map(subject => subject.label));
const tracks = new Intl.ListFormat('en', { style: 'long', type: 'conjunction' })
  .format(library.tracks.map(track => track.label));
---

<StarlightPage
  headings={headings}
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'About',
    description: "About zzj's personal notebook for mathematics and physics: Typst exposition, Lean 4 formal proofs, and computational models.",
    editUrl: false,
  }}
>
  <article class="about-page">
    <header class="about-intro">
      <p class="about-kicker"><span aria-hidden="true">∴</span> ABOUT THIS NOTEBOOK</p>
      <p class="about-lead">I'm zzj. This is where I turn intuition — mathematical and physical — into arguments I can return to, question, and refine.</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="why-this-notebook-exists">
      <p class="about-section-number" aria-hidden="true">01</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="why-this-notebook-exists">Why this notebook exists</h2>
        <p>Mathematics and physics become clearer when an idea is written precisely enough to be checked. I use this site to record that process in both directions: beginning with a picture, a question or a physical situation, following the definitions, and keeping the reasoning that connects them.</p>
        <p>These pages are written first as notes to my future self. Publishing them makes the work easier to revisit and leaves a useful trail for anyone studying the same ideas.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="how-i-work">
      <p class="about-section-number" aria-hidden="true">02</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="how-i-work">How I work</h2>
        <p>I write the exposition, the mathematics and the physical derivations in Typst. When an argument benefits from machine-checked certainty, I use Lean 4 to make every assumption and inference explicit.</p>
        <p>Formalization is not a replacement for intuition, and intuition is not a replacement for proof. The most useful notes let the two correct each other.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="about-principle">
      <span aria-hidden="true">∎</span>
      <p>Understand the idea.<br />State it precisely.<br />Check what survives.</p>
    </aside>

    <section aria-labelledby="what-you-will-find">
      <p class="about-section-number" aria-hidden="true">03</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="what-you-will-find">What you'll find</h2>
        <p>The notebook currently gathers {library.total} {library.total === 1 ? 'note' : 'notes'} under {library.subjects.length} {library.subjects.length === 1 ? 'subject' : 'subjects'} in {library.tracks.length} parallel {library.tracks.length === 1 ? 'track' : 'tracks'} — {tracks}. The subjects are {subjects}. Some entries develop a concept from definitions to proofs; others derive a physical result, connect exposition with formal verification, or work through a small computational model.</p>
        <p>Mathematics and physics are kept side by side rather than mixed together, so each line can be read on its own: every subject belongs to exactly one track, and the sidebar, the index and the track pages all say which. This is a working notebook rather than a finished textbook. Notes may grow as my understanding changes, while the derivations, references, and source remain visible.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="open-notebook">
      <p class="about-section-number" aria-hidden="true">04</p>
      <div>
        <h2 id="open-notebook">An open notebook</h2>
        <p>Each note is available for reading on the web, with PDF and Typst editions where applicable. The notes are shared under CC BY-SA 4.0, and their source is public for study, reuse, and correction.</p>
        <div class="note-tools">
          <a class="primary-link" href="/">Browse the notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a href="https://github.com/zzjrabbit/notes">View the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</StarlightPage>
